# Paths @expo/fingerprint must not hash, on top of its own defaults.
#
# The runtime version is `fingerprint`, so every file hashed here has to be
# byte-identical on this laptop and on EAS's clean checkout. When they differ,
# `eas build` stops at "Configure expo-updates" with a runtime version mismatch,
# and — worse, because it is silent — an `eas update` published from the laptop
# is stamped with a runtime version no installed build has, so it reaches
# nobody. See docs/MOBILE_RELEASE.md §3.3.
#
# Eclipse/Buildship writes these into *every* Gradle subproject it imports, and
# the autolinked native modules under node_modules are subprojects of
# `android/`. They are IDE bookkeeping — nothing in the build reads them — but
# fingerprint's defaults only skip `android/build`, `android/.gradle` and
# `android/.cxx`, so without these three lines an IDE import of the Android
# project silently moves the runtime version of ten packages.
**/.classpath
**/.project
**/.settings/**/*
